{"baseRefName":"main","baseRefOid":"0f821bb5a7d9655a99a967a70dfb38ed329bf014","body":"Normal Core reports now have an explicit contract for captured Let values, immediate state updates, statement-local effects and empty actions. This adds six child clauses under existing UNI requirements and two public CLI tests covering five independently frozen Counter and empty-action reports. No production code or dependency changes.\n\nLocal validation: both tests passed all five CLI calls, comparing complete JSON and exact stdout/stderr bytes plus exit status. Counter runs unmetered, at cap16 and at u128::MAX; empty action runs unmetered and at cap0 while preserving its complete state, balances and liability. The one offline/frozen, cold-target, single-job command completed in 53.785 seconds under a 90-second bound plus five seconds termination grace. Exact source/tree/logs/cleanup and independent source/result reviews are retained on the utxo evidence branch.\n\nThe fixtures were derived independently after the disclosed design adoption. Existing Transfer mori-test aggregate bytes retain their separate consumer and freeze. Full eleven-node parser correspondence, default/native/workspace/compiler/proof/ledger checks and all parent EARS exits remain open. No historical test counts are combined into a current whole-suite pass.\n","closedAt":"2026-10-18T08:01:39Z","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-10-18T07:40:03Z","authors":[{"email":"charles.hoskinson@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNzk5NTI=","login":"CharlesHoskinson","name":"Charles Hoskinson"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-18T07:40:16Z","messageBody":"Adopted design and independently frozen expectations only; full candidate review and five-call runtime validation remain pending.","messageHeadline":"Specify complete Core reports and add independent positive CLI cases","oid":"00667c466548b654b9e9ca02ebdbd009fbc08948"}],"createdAt":"2026-10-18T07:40:19Z","files":[{"path":"crates/fixtures/core-report-contract/CASES.json","additions":104,